# Legacy Alembic migration history

The Alembic revisions in this directory are retained for databases created by
the former Python backend. Revisions `0001` through `0010` are historical
records and must remain available because some deployed databases may already
have applied them. `0001` through `0005` describe the pre-Rust baseline;
`0006` through `0010` are later legacy changes that are not executed by the
production Rust image.

The production Rust image does not execute Alembic. The Rust backend bootstraps
fresh databases from `sql/0001_initial.sql`, accepts databases upgraded through
the legacy Alembic history, and is the only forward schema owner beginning
with `rust_schema_versions` version 3. Do not add new Alembic revisions; add
future schema upgrades to both the fresh-install SQL and the Rust upgrade path,
with PostgreSQL integration coverage.
